Package: DRCRTwa
Type: Package
Title: Doubly Robust While-Alive Estimation for Randomized Trials
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Xi", "Fang", email = "xfang@mcw.edu", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Da", "Zhao", email = "dzhao@yale.edu", role = "aut"),
    person("Fan", "Li", email = "fan.f.li@yale.edu", role = "aut")
  )
Description: Estimates exposure-weighted while-alive recurrent-event rates in
    individually randomized and cluster-randomized trials with a terminal event
    and covariate-dependent censoring. The compiled implementation fits
    arm-specific Cox working models for censoring and terminal events and
    Lin-Wei-Yang-Ying marginal proportional-rate working models for recurrent
    event types. It combines inverse probability of censoring weighting,
    outcome-regression augmentation, censoring-martingale correction, and
    independent-unit influence-function inference. Multiple recurrent-event
    types can be combined through prespecified nonnegative clinical weights,
    and cluster-randomized analyses can report individual-average and
    cluster-average estimands.
